Harbor: mshtml: a script from a file marked "defer" runs after the document is parsed (#100).

mshtml ran every script where Gecko's parser handed it over, the deferred ones included, so a deferred
script in the head ran before the body existed. Pages rely on the opposite: Office's add-in Store page loads
its three scripts with defer from the head and then looks for the element in the body it renders into
("Root container missing").

A script element with defer and a src that turns up while the document is still loading is now queued and
run, in document order, when Gecko reports the end of the load, before the document becomes interactive.
Inline scripts and scripts added after loading are run as before. Not handled: async.

Test: WindowsTests/mshtml.

